-- V5__seed_firm40_closure.sql
--
-- Referential-closure seed around the firm-40 rows from V4. Round 1: starting
-- from the already-seeded firm-40 entities (advisor/household/clients) and their
-- accounts, follow the key columns (ENTITY_ID, NF_ACCOUNT_ID) to the related
-- tables and seed <=10 matching rows from each, so the firm-40 record graph is
-- filled out (addresses, phones, tax/billing data, balances/values, transactions,
-- ebaskets, proposals, perf, service requests, dashboards, permissions, ...).
--
-- Provenance : real PROD rows (192.168.1.42/ORCL12VM, GP), PII-SCRUBBED with the
--              Faker library (db/tools/scrub_faker.py): every PII column value
--              (names, emails, phones, addresses, tax ids, account numbers, ...)
--              is replaced by a realistic, deterministic-per-value fake; IDs,
--              codes, dates, flags and keys stay real, so referential coherence
--              is preserved. Repo is public.
-- Generated  : 2026-06-01. Applies on top of V1-V4 (Flyway migrate -> v5).
--
-- Bounding: expansion follows the SPECIFIC key VALUES of seeded rows (this
-- household/clients/accounts), not firm_cd=40 wholesale; <=10 rows per table;
-- views, materialized views, temp/backup tables and ISEQ$$ are skipped.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
